To add the RNFR and CWD commands to the sequence of client requests, we need to place them in the appropriate context. The RNFR command is used to specify the name of the file or directory you want to rename, and it is typically followed by the RNTO command to specify the new name. The CWD command is used to change the working directory.

Assuming you want to rename a directory after listing its contents, we can modify the sequence as follows:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
LIST
RNFR old_directory_name  ; Specify the directory you want to rename
CWD new_directory_name    ; Change to the new directory if needed
RNTO new_directory_name   ; Specify the new name for the directory
QUIT
```

If you need a specific context for the RNFR and CWD commands, please provide additional details, and I can adjust the sequence accordingly

